---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ServiceCard from '../components/ServiceCard.astro';
import { healthCheck, implementationServices } from '../data/services';
---

<Base
  title="Pricing"
  description="Transparent starting prices for the OriginsLynk Automation Health Check, Core System, Expanded System, and Managed System services."
>
  <section class="section-cream page-hero">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Straightforward pricing</p>
      <h1>Know the starting point before the sales call.</h1>
      <p class="lede">You receive a written fixed scope and price before work begins. The right recommendation may be a small setup, a diagnostic, a larger system—or no build at all.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pricing-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="service-grid">
        <ServiceCard service={healthCheck} label="Diagnose existing automation" featured />
        {implementationServices.map((service, index) => (
          <ServiceCard service={service} label={`${index + 1} · ${index === 0 ? 'Two workflows' : index === 1 ? 'Four total workflows' : 'Six total workflows'}`} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sunken">
    <div class="container price-details">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What changes the price</p>
        <h2>Complexity is priced before it becomes your surprise.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="factor-grid">
        <article><h3>More Health Check workflows</h3><p>The $350 Health Check covers up to three workflows on one automation platform. Additional workflows start at $100 each.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Additional implementation workflows</h3><p>Implementation starts at $125. Standard templated workflows are typically $125–$250 and include up to two supported app connections. Additional connections or complexity are quoted separately.</p></article>
        <article><h3>More platforms</h3><p>A second automation platform adds $200 to a Health Check, and workflow-count pricing still applies across the full audit. Multiple business accounts inside one workflow are evaluated during scope.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Missing evidence</h3><p>Missing documentation or unusable run history may add $100–$250 because the system must first be reconstructed.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Unusual risk or complexity</h3><p>Advanced branching, custom code, high volume, unfamiliar systems, or regulated information requires a custom quote or may be declined.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="care-plan" class="section-dark care-section">
    <div class="container care-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Tier 3 ongoing care</p>
        <h2>$250 per month beginning day 31</h2>
        <p class="lede">This required monthly plan covers the dedicated OriginsLynk-managed workflow server and the work required to keep the agreed environment maintained.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Included</h3>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Managed workflow server use and remote administration</li>
          <li>Automated monitoring and backup verification</li>
          <li>Routine maintenance and failure investigation</li>
          <li>Weekly review of server health, backup results, and workflow execution records</li>
          <li>Monthly service report and business-hours support</li>
          <li>Up to 30 minutes of minor workflow adjustments each month</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Quoted separately</h3>
        <ul class="crosslist">
          <li>New workflows, integrations, or major changes</li>
          <li>After-hours emergency response</li>
          <li>Third-party subscriptions and usage charges</li>
          <li>Guaranteed uptime or detection of every failure</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container upgrade-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Upgrade without buying the same work twice</p>
        <h2>Compatible completed setup is credited toward the next tier.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">A completed Tier 1 setup can receive a $750 credit toward Tier 2 or Tier 3, and a completed Tier 2 setup can receive a $1,200 credit toward Tier 3, after a compatibility review. Remediation, changed requirements, and new scope are quoted separately.</p>
        <div class="btn-row"><a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Request a service</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero h1 { max-width: 16ch; }
  .page-hero .lede { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .service-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); }
  .price-details, .upgrade-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-8); }
  .price-details h2, .upgrade-grid h2 { max-width: 16ch; }
  .factor-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); }
  .factor-grid article { padding-top: var(--space-5); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); }
  .factor-grid h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .factor-grid p { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .care-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-7); }
  .care-grid h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .care-grid .lede { margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .section-dark .checklist li, .section-dark .crosslist li { color: var(--ink-inverse-muted); }
  .section-dark .checklist li::before { border-color: #8fd0c6; }
  @media (min-width: 42em) {
    .service-grid, .factor-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (min-width: 64em) {
    .service-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
    .price-details, .upgrade-grid { grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; }
    .care-grid { grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
